        }
      },
      "means": {
        "2048": 0.6969,
        "4096": 0.7107,
        "16384": 0.4423
      },
      "reading": "2048 and 4096 differ by 0.014 on n=7, far inside the established 0.10 materiality scale and not separable at this sample size. The plugin's own preferred block of 16384 is clearly worse here, which is expected: 16384 samples is 1024 ms at 16 kHz, and the plugin's defaults were designed for 44.1 kHz where that block is 372 ms.",
      "block_16384_would_also_have_been_wrong_for_a_movement_probe": "16384 samples = 32 hops, so two states 8 hops apart would share 75 percent of their window content and movement would be mechanically suppressed - a false-positive risk for a restraint probe.",
      "REPORTED_NOT_GATED": true
    }
  },
  "alignment_rule": {
    "the_problem": "the plugin timestamps each feature at its BLOCK START. host_chroma12 uses a TRAILING CAUSAL window: host frame i covers samples [(i+1)*512 - 2048, (i+1)*512).",
    "the_rule": "host_frame_index = plugin_frame_index + (B/512 - 1), which is +3 at block 2048",
    "derivation": "plugin frame j covers [j*512, j*512 + B), ending at j*512 + B. Host frame i ends at (i+1)*512. Setting the window ENDS equal gives (i+1)*512 = j*512 + B, hence i = j + B/512 - 1. This is an exact integer shift; no interpolation, no resampling, no data fitting.",
    "leading_frames": "the first (B/512 - 1) = 3 host frames have no corresponding plugin frame and are excluded by the validity mask. They are not zero-filled.",
    "verification_performed": "a synthetic note onset at a known sample index appears at the predicted plugin frame at blocks 2048, 4096 and 16384, and both arms produce identical timing.",
    "DISCLOSED_EMPIRICAL_SCAN": {
      "what": "an integer shift sweep 0..8 maximising pitch-class cosine against the MIDI target on 5 stems",
      "result_best_shift_per_stem": [
        1,
        2,
        2,
        2,
        0
      ],
      "spread_over_shifts_0_to_3_on_the_worst_case": 0.005,
      "decision": "the DETERMINISTIC GEOMETRIC RULE (+3) is pre-registered, NOT the empirical optimum. The empirical optimum is data-selected on the scoring corpus and the difference is immaterial (0.005 cosine). Fitting the alignment to the corpus would be exactly the kind of quiet tuning this programme forbids.",
      "why_the_empirical_optimum_sits_1_to_2_frames_earlier": "the MIDI target is a rectangular duration-occupancy measure and the whitened spectrum has its own onset and decay behaviour, so the cosine optimum blends onset alignment with sustain overlap. This is the same rectangular-oracle effect J3I characterised and it is not evidence against the geometric rule.",
      "REPORTED_NOT_GATED": true
    }
  },
  "arms": {
    "design_note": "the contrast the brief asks for exists INSIDE the published implementation and does not require us to hand-roll anything. Both arms run the identical front end - log-frequency spectrum at 3 bins per semitone, tuning, spectral whitening - and diverge at exactly one branch in NNLSChroma.cpp (line 359, 'if (m_useNNLS == 0)').",
    "ARM_F_FRONTEND_ONLY": {
      "useNNLS": 0.0,
      "what_the_published_code_does": "maps the whitened tuned log-frequency spectrum to 84 semitone bins by a triangular-weighted sum over the 3 bins per semitone. Linear energy mapping. NO transcription, NO dictionary, NO non-negative least squares.",
      "what_it_isolates": "the value of the RESOLVED, TUNED, WHITENED front end on its own - the J3N hypothesis, now measured in a second independent implementation"
    },
    "ARM_N_NNLS_NOTES": {
      "useNNLS": 1.0,
      "what_the_published_code_does": "solves a non-negative least squares problem against a dictionary of harmonic note templates (geometric partial amplitude series, s = 0.7) over the significant semitone positions, yielding 84 approximate note activations.",
      "what_it_isolates": "the value of harmonic-dictionary ATTRIBUTION on top of that front end - the J3O hypothesis"
    },
    "single_variable_changed": "useNNLS. Nothing else. Same binary, same parameters, same block, same step, same alignment, same fold, same normalisation, same movement metric."
  },
  "execution_environment": "Anthropic cloud container (HOST-class). BabySlakh 16 kHz, md5 verified against the publisher's checksum.",
