    "_CAVEAT": {
      "status": "these fixtures were RUN BEFORE this pre-registration was written, during toolchain validation. Their results are therefore not blind and they are DIAGNOSTIC ONLY - no outcome depends on them.",
      "what_was_seen": "on the synthetic 1/h harmonic stacks the plugin's semitone spectrum places only 0.22 to 0.42 of its mass on the correct note, and MIDI 84 fails outright (0.075 to 0.103).",
      "diagnosis_established_before_pre_registration": "this is block-invariant (tested 4096, 8192, 16384, 32768) AND sample-rate-invariant (tested 16000, 22050 and 44100 Hz, the plugin's design rate), so it is NOT a rate or window mismatch. On real audio with known per-stem MIDI the same configuration achieves pitch-class cosine 0.62 to 0.89. The conclusion is that a mathematically exact 1/h harmonic stack is a PATHOLOGICAL input for a spectrally-whitened NNLS with a fixed geometric dictionary at s = 0.7 - the running-mean-and-standard-deviation whitening has no spectral irregularity to key on, and the perfectly regular stack matches many dictionary atoms almost equally.",
      "how_it_must_be_read": "the fixtures are reported exactly as briefed, and they MUST NOT be read as a plugin failure or as evidence about real-audio behaviour. The corpus probe is the evidence."
    }
