  "reliability_diagnostic": {
    "what_was_asked_for": "the NNLS fit residual, as a reported reliability diagnostic",
    "finding": "NOT FAITHFULLY OBSERVABLE through the published plugin",
    "evidence": "the residual norm is computed at NNLSChroma.cpp line 386 (declaration) and line 399 (the nnls() call writes it into rnorm), and is then NEVER READ. None of the plugin's six outputs (logfreqspec, tunedlogfreqspec, semitonespectrum, chroma, basschroma, bothchroma) carries it.",
    "declared_outcome": "NNLS_RELIABILITY_NOT_OBSERVED",
    "no_proxy_will_be_manufactured": true,
    "why_not_reconstructed_externally": "the residual is ||D*x - b||, and while b (tunedlogfreqspec) and x (semitonespectrum) are both exposed, the dictionary D is internal. Reimplementing D from the source would be a reconstruction of our own, not the published quantity, and getting it subtly wrong would produce a confident-looking number that means nothing.",
    "available_follow_up_if_the_PM_WANTS_IT": "exposing rnorm would be a one-line addition to the GPL research host plus one extra Vamp output. That is a separate authorisation and has NOT been done.",
    "observed_outcome": "NNLS_RELIABILITY_NOT_OBSERVED"
  },
